<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 82,055 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 82,055 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 82,055 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday compared to 59,685 tonnes in the same period on Monday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Tuesday     Jan 13</p>
<p>    Export cargo		11,320	 5,583</p>
<p>    Import cargo		70,735	54,102</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, nine are expected to sail and 10 are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 25,000	 Miraj		 14/1</p>
<p>Sugar		    13,125	 Harmony Breeze    15/1</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     25,210	 Iktinos	     17/1</p>
<p>Vehicles		    109	 Freccia	     Due</p>
<p>Vehicles		    100	 Hual Favorite     20/1</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
